{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Each of your creatures gets "speed attacker".
{DRAGON EVADE} (When this creature would leave the battle zone, flip it to the fortress side instead.)

{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Each of your creatures gets "speed attacker".
{DRAGON EVADE} (When this creature would leave the battle zone, flip it to the fortress side instead.)

{SPEED ATTACKER} (This creature doesn't get summoning sickness.)
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Whenever this creature attacks or whenever your opponent chooses this creature, put a dragheart creature that costs 10 or less from your hyperspatial zone. That creature gets "speed attacker" until the end of the turn.

■ Dragsolution: When the equipped creature would leave by the effect of one of your opponent's spells or creature ability, flip this dragheart to the creature side and untap it instead.
{HYPERSPATIAL DRAGHEART}
■ Dragsolution: At the start of your turn, if you have 2 or more fire creatures in the battle zone, flip this card to the dragheart creature side and untap it. (At the start of your game, draghearts are put into your hyperspatial zone. If a creature equipped with it or the dragheart leaves the battle zone, return it there.)

{DOUBLE BREAKER}
{MANA ARMS} 5: When you put this creature, if you have 5 or more fire cards in your mana zone, put a fire dragheart that costs 5 or less from your hyperspatial zone. (If it's a weapon, equip it to this creature.)
■ Dragon Mana Arms 5: When this creature attacks for the first time in a turn, if you have 5 or more fire Dragons in your mana zone, untap this creature after the attack.

{SPEED ATTACKER} (This creature doesn't get summoning sickness.)
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Whenever this creature attacks or whenever your opponent chooses this creature, put a dragheart creature that costs 10 or less from your hyperspatial zone. That creature gets "speed attacker" until the end of the turn.

{JUSTDIVER} (When you put this creature, it can't be chosen by your opponent and can't be attacked until the start of your next turn.)
{DOUBLE BREAKER}
■ When you put this creature or at the start of your turn, draw 2 cards and put a card from your hand into your hyperspatial zone. Then you may put an element that costs the same as or less the number of dragon cards in your mana zone from your hyperspatial zone. If it's a weapon, equip it to this creature.
